1
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:42,000
An epic adventure and passionate romance unfold against the
panorama of a frontier wilderness ravaged by war.

2
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:18,000
The Last of the Mohicans is a action, history,
romance film directed by Michael Mann.

3
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:54,000
In war-torn colonial America, in the midst of a bloody battle between British, the French and Native American allies,
the aristocratic daughter of a British Colonel and her party are captured by a group of Huron warriors.

4
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:30,000
Fortunately, a group of three Mohican trappers comes to their rescue.

5
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Hawkeye, played by Daniel Day-Lewis.

6
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:42,000
Cora, played by Madeleine Stowe.

7
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:18,000
Alice, played by Jodhi May.

8
00:44:48,000 --> 00:44:54,000
Chingachgook, played by Russell Means.

9
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:30,000
Magua, played by Wes Studi.

10
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
Uncas, played by Eric Schweig.

11
01:01:36,000 --> 01:01:42,000
The Last of the Mohicans is a 1992 American epic historical drama war film co-produced and directed by Michael Mann, who co-wrote the
screenplay with Christopher Crowe, based on the 1826 novel of the same name by James Fenimore Cooper and its 1936 film adaptation.

12
01:07:12,000 --> 01:07:18,000
The film is set in 1757 during the French and Indian War.

13
01:12:48,000 --> 01:12:54,000
It stars Daniel Day-Lewis, Madeleine Stowe, and Jodhi May in the leading roles, and features Russell
Means, Wes Studi, Eric Schweig, Steven Waddington, Maurice Roëves, and Patrice Chéreau.

14
01:18:24,000 --> 01:18:30,000
The film was released in the United States on September 25, 1992.

15
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
It received generally positive reviews from
critics and was a commercial success.

16
01:29:36,000 --> 01:29:42,000
It won the Academy Award for Best Sound, the only Academy
Award won by a film directed by Mann to date.

17
01:35:12,000 --> 01:35:18,000
It was also nominated for seven BAFTA Awards, including Best Actor in a Leading Role
for Day-Lewis, and won Best Cinematography and Best Make-up Artist.

18
01:40:48,000 --> 01:40:54,000
The film explores themes of based on novel or book, love triangle,
native american, revenge, interracial relationship.

19
01:46:24,000 --> 01:46:30,000
The tone is emotional.
